{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Morning, let's get a blood pressure before the doctor calls you. Arm out straight for me.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Ok.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): One thirty eight over eighty four, pulse 76. Any allergies I should flag?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): None that we know of. I'm Linda, his wife. He wouldn't have come if I hadn't booked it, his hands have been awful.",
  "[SEG0006] person_4 (DOCTOR): Sorry, give me a second, the screen's frozen again. Right, Mr Hale, what brings you in?",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): Hands.",
  "[SEG0008] person_4 (DOCTOR): Hands. Say that again, I was on the wrong tab.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): Numb.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Both hands go numb in the night, the thumb and the two fingers next to it. He sits up and shakes them till they wake up.",
  "[SEG0011] person_4 (DOCTOR): Shakes them. Umm, how long has this been going on?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Months.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I thought February, or actually it might've been before Christmas, I can't quite...",
  "[SEG0014] person_4 (DOCTOR): Hang on, the cursor's jumped. Sorry, when did you say it started?",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I honestly can't pin the date. Months, anyway. And he's been dropping things.",
  "[SEG0016] person_4 (DOCTOR): Dropping what?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): Cups.",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Tea mugs at home, and the little parts on the line. He packs at the factory, days and nights.",
  "[SEG0019] person_4 (DOCTOR): Right. Is there pain with it, or just the numb feeling?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Numb.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): No pain, he's told me, just dead numb. Worse after a night shift.",
  "[SEG0022] person_4 (DOCTOR): Ok. Any fever with all this?",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0024] person_4 (DOCTOR): Sorry, the fever, say it again, I didn't catch it.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0026] person_4 (DOCTOR): Any cough?",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0028] person_4 (DOCTOR): And your weight, has that changed at all?",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): Dunno.",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He's up and down. Belt's the same I think, but he won't get on the scales, so...",
  "[SEG0031] person_4 (DOCTOR): Not very clear then. Any chest pain?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0033] person_4 (DOCTOR): Are you taking anything for the hands?",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He was on naproxin, 500 milligrams twice a day, but he stopped it in March. It burned his stomach.",
  "[SEG0035] person_4 (DOCTOR): Naproxen, five hundred milligrams twice a day, stopped in March. There was gabapentin on an old letter, did he ever take that?",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): Never.",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Box is still sealed in the cupboard. He wouldn't touch it.",
  "[SEG0038] person_4 (DOCTOR): So never started, I'll leave it. What do you actually take now? The medication list on here is a mess, say it again.",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (PATIENT): Statin.",
  "[SEG0040] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Atorvastatin, twenty milligrams at night, for his cholesterol. Years now.",
  "[SEG0041] person_4 (DOCTOR): Twenty at night, got it. Sensation's a bit dull over the thumb and the next two fingers, both hands. Tapping the right wrist brings on a tingle, that's a positive Tinel's.",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): Mm.",
  "[SEG0043] person_4 (DOCTOR): Err, my working impression is carpal tunnel, not proven yet. Wear a wrist splint at night, both wrists, for six weeks. If it hasn't settled with the splints we might send you for nerve conduction studies.",
  "[SEG0044] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Do we come back anyway, or only if the splints...",
  "[SEG0045] person_4 (DOCTOR): Book six weeks with reception on your way out, that's definite. The nerve test only if the splints haven't sorted it."
 ],
